      "writtenOn": "2018-03-19T16:23:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Whups.\n\nI guess we do need to make a copy of the params in here.  Because chip_i2c_xfer() could alter out and out_size, and then this repeated call would send down different params.\n\nstruct i2c_xfer_params pcopy \u003d *p;\nret \u003d chip_i2c_xfer(\u0026pcopy);\n\nOn the plus side, that means that callers of i2c_xfer() don\u0027t need to worry about making that copy themselves when they call it repeatedly from the same struct.  That simplifies the logic for the top-level caller, which is good because that\u0027s what we\u0027d mess up later when we forgot that i2c_xfer() mutated the entire struct.\n\nOoooh, and that means that i2c_xfer can take a const struct *.  Which is how we differentiate it from the sub-functions that take a mutable struct.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 98,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "acd4b8ca5a2f6feff2c4a291b0f51c4f32d9d94f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
